-- title:
--   Power relations with degree drop imply module finiteness
-- statement:
--   If each coordinate has a positive power relation whose coefficients have weighted degree lower by the same positive amount D, then the polynomial ring is finite over the algebra generated by the relation polynomials.
-- source:
--   openai/math Ampleness stack: WeightedIdealCurveBound implies eps-ample exceptional twist, hence Serre vanishing and eventual generation of I^n by weight ≤ n(rho+eps) sections.

